  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 208 PM EDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nMain changes from recent forecasts was somewhat higher\nconfidence in main axis of storms and impacts of heat/humidity\nTue-Wed.\n\nScattered to at times numerous showers have dotted the skies\nthrough the morning, with the main area slowly starting to shift\neast. Additional development appears to be trying to expand\nin portions of NW IL to west central Lower MI in association\nwith a weak mid-level wave. Models doing poorly on handling \nthis, so confidence regarding evolution on the lower side. \nSuspect at least some CIN should be in place with the morning \nshowers, but a pocket of clearing is noted that may help \novercome some of that. Most likely this will remain west and\nnorth of the area, but trends will need to be watched for\npossible inclusion of pops in NW areas. \n\nFocus then shifts to concerns for heat and humidity as upper\nlevel ridge builds north and shifts the axis of showers/storms\ninto WI/MI through mid week. Models seem to be leaning towards\nthis trend, but concerns still linger some given low confidence\nin model handling of subsequent waves and pops. Also, SPC has\nmaintained the Marginal Risk for severe storms across the\nnorthern half of the area (possibly overdone). After much \ncollaboration, it was decided to hoist a Heat Advisory from 16Z \nTue through 00Z Thu for all of northern Indiana and northwestern\nOhio where the greatest confidence exists for heat indices of \naround 100 degrees to possibly as high as 105 degrees. Greatest \nconfidence does exist on Wed for criteria being met, but close \nenough to just go with both days. Concerns could linger across \nsouthern areas Thursday, but was decided to defer to later \nforecasts. \n\nThereafter, additional chances for convection and/or heat\nconcerns will hinge on the position of the upper level ridge\nresulting in sporadic pops into the weekend and somewhat cooler\ntemperatures.",
